    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face an advantageous slate today, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (76.88) and **Trea Turner** (72.88). **Junior Caminero** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft 4.92 xERA matchup against Stock; his 19% boost in SP Skill efficiency positions him for high-ceiling production. Similarly, **Trea Turner** remains a category-anchor due to his elite sprint speed and a favorable 4.36 xERA matchup against Pfaadt. While **Kyle Schwarber** (69.43) and **Yordan Alvarez** (68.77) boast high raw outputs, the combination of **Hector Rodriguez** (65.93) and **Christian Yelich** (65.59) provides critical stability; **Christian Yelich** in particular sees a 13% platoon efficiency boost, making him a high-floor selection despite a minor penalty for the opponent\u2019s ability to hold runners.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved the utility slot, where **Carson Benge** (33.26) was considered but ultimately benched. Despite his potential, his poor matchup against Seymour (3.19 xERA) and a negative platoon split (L/L) caused his efficiency to plummet well below our 40.0 floor, keeping him off the active roster in favor of the more favorable matchups for **Colt Keith** (59.72) and **Lars Nootbaar** (55.87). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (45.43) is the primary risk factor for the Zebras today; his score was heavily suppressed by Harrison\u2019s high-quality profile (3.07 xERA) and the negative impact of a tough lefty-lefty platoon. We will monitor the lineup of **Dillon Dingler** (41.82) closely, as his low efficiency is sensitive to his recent struggle against right-handed pitching; should the wind shift or late-inning replacements materialize for **Gary Sanchez** or **Casey Schmitt**, we may look to pivot if his base projections shift negatively before first pitch.",
